# GitCode

A lightweight self-hosted Git platform, built from scratch in Python and React.

**Status:** Beta. Not ready for production.

## What is GitCode

GitCode is a self-hosted alternative to GitHub, designed to run on Termux/Android
without root. It stores real git repositories on disk and serves them through a
small HTTP API and a React web interface.

## Features

| Feature | Status |
|---------|--------|
| User signup / login | Done |
| Create / delete repositories | Done |
| Browse repo tree, files, commits | Done |
| Branches | Done |
| README.gc rendering | Done |
| LICENSE tab | Done |
| Fork repositories | Done |
| Clone menu (HTTPS / SSH / CLI) | Done |
| Issues | Planned |
| Pull requests | Planned |
| Stars / watch | Planned |
| Web editor | Planned |
| Search | Planned |

## Architecture

    Browser (React + Tailwind)
            |
            v
    Python HTTP API (backend/server.py)
            |
            +--> auth.py       (sessions, pbkdf2)
            +--> db.py         (SQLite)
            +--> git_ops.py    (git CLI wrapper)
            |
            v
    data/gitcode.db   +   repos/<user>/<repo>.git/

## Requirements

- Python 3.10+
- Node.js 18+
- git CLI

## Setup

### Backend

    cd backend
    python server.py
    # http://localhost:8080

### Frontend

    cd frontend
    npm install
    npm run dev -- --host 0.0.0.0 --port 5173
    # http://localhost:5173

### CLI

    ln -sf ~/gitcode/cli/gc ~/bin/gc
    gc login
    gc create my-project
    gc push
    gc clone user/repo
    gc fork user/repo

## CLI reference

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `gc login` | Log in to a server |
| `gc logout` | Clear local session |
| `gc whoami` | Print current user |
| `gc create <name>` | Create a repository |
| `gc list` | List your repositories |
| `gc push` | Push current directory to server |
| `gc clone <user>/<repo>` | Clone a repository |
| `gc fork <user>/<repo>` | Fork a repository |
| `gc config` | Show or set config |

## Custom README

GitCode looks for `README.gc` first, falling back to `README.md`.
The same applies to `LICENSE`, `LICENSE.md`, `LICENSE.gc`.

